            <div xml:id="d539">

                <pb facs="0442" n="430" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.6282/52: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hibbard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-05T11:00:00-00:44">November 5,
                            1942—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:33 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>373. Gottfried von Waldheim German Consul General accompanied by Franz Noelke
                    Vice Consul and Carl Heinzbrand clerk left Monrovia this morning at 11 o’clock
                    by French plane for Abidjan, French Ivory Coast. Tomorrow at 10 o’clock they
                    will leave Abidjan by train for Bobo-Dioulasso, where on November 10 they will
                    take a French commercial plane for Algiers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hibbard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
